  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 91036662a85844eb162bdfbe2ea8ce9c, type: 3}
  m_Name: TurkishRules
  m_EditorClassIdentifier:
  displayName: Turkish
  description: Dama - pieces move in straight lines on every square, flying kings, mandatory capture.
  longDescription: "<b>Board Size & Setup</b>\nPlayed on a standard 8x8 grid (64 squares). Unlike western checkers, both light and dark squares are used, and color does not matter for movement. Each player starts with 16 pieces, completely filling the second and third rows closest to each player - the very first row and the middle two rows are left empty.\n\n<b>Basic Movement</b>\nOrthogonal Only: pieces never move diagonally. Three Directions: regular pieces can move one square forward, left, or right - they cannot move backward.\n\n<b>Capture Mechanics & Strict Hierarchy</b>\nCapturing is mandatory, with an intense maximum-capture rule: 1) Maximum Quantity - if you have multiple jumping paths available, you must choose the path that captures the highest number of pieces. Orthogonal Jumps: capture an enemy piece by jumping over it in a straight line (forward, left, or right) into an empty space directly behind it - no diagonal jumps. Immediate Removal: captured pieces are removed from the board immediately as they're jumped, which frequently opens up new paths mid-turn. No 180-Degree Turns: during a single multi-jump turn, you cannot jump a piece, turn around, and jump backward through the square you just left.\n\n<b>The Dama (King)</b>\nPromotion: when a regular piece reaches the 8th row, it turns into a Dama. Orthogonal Flying King: a Dama can slide any number of empty squares forward, backward, left, or right in a straight line. Long-Range Jumps: a Dama can fly across any distance of empty squares to jump an isolated enemy piece, landing on any empty square behind it.\n\n<b>Winning the Game</b>\nElimination or Blockade: you win by capturing all 16 of your opponent's pieces or trapping them so they have zero legal moves left. The End-Game Rule: if one player is reduced to just a single regular piece while the other still has a Dama, the player with the Dama instantly wins."
  rows: 8
  columns: 8
  pieceRowsPerSide: 2
  movementScheme: 1
  piecesOnAllSquares: 1
  leaveBackRowEmpty: 1
  flyingKings: 1
  menCaptureBackward: 1
  menCannotCaptureKings: 0
  mustCaptureMaximum: 1
  preferKingMover: 0
  preferKingCaptures: 0
  preferEarlierKingCapture: 0
  midChainPromotionRule: 0
  deferCaptureRemoval: 0
  forbidImmediateReversal: 1
  noProgressMoveLimit: 30
  singleManLosesToKing: 1
